/* book: lead: A convolutional code does not cut the message into independent blocks. It feeds each input bit through a shift register, so one input bit shapes several output bits. The encoder is simple; the decoder must search. Viterbi decoding finds the trellis path whose coded bits are closest to the received bits. These codes appear in satellite modems, deep-space links, voice-band modems and the convolution */
/* book Figure 7.8.1: The trellis of worked example 1. Each circle holds the smallest path metric into that state; the thick path, traced back from 00 at the end, costs only 1 (at the fourth pair, where the channel flipped a bit) and decodes to 1011. */
