/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Write the code as (n, k, K).
   - R is the code rate, dimensionless; k is input bits per step; n is output bits per step.
   - The rate 1/2, K = 3 encoder has two delay cells.
   - u(i) is the input bit at step i; u(i−1) and u(i−2) are stored past bits; ⊕ is modulo-2 addition; c1(i) and c2(i) are the two output bits.
   - The generator sequences are g1 = 111 and g2 = 101.
   - The state is the last K − 1 input bits, written u(i−1)u(i−2).
   - The code tree unrolls the same diagram in time.
   - To end at state 00, append K − 1 = 2 zero bits after the message.
   - Viterbi decoding is maximum-likelihood sequence detection for a memoryless channel.
   - Each stage does about 2K−1 compare-select operations.
*/
