/* book exam traps: Treating K as the memory. The constraint length is K = memory + 1, so a two-cell encoder has K = 3. | Forgetting the K − 1 flush bits, so the trellis never returns to state 00 and the final state is unknown. | Mixing branch metric with path metric. A branch metric covers one trellis stage; a path metric is the accumulated sum. | Using 2K states in the trellis. The state count is 2K−1. | Using Hamming distance for soft-decision decoding. Soft decisions need Euclidean distance or a correlation measure. */
