/* book: lead: Shannon proved codes can come close to capacity. BCH codes are cyclic codes with a guaranteed minimum distance. Turbo codes run two convolutional encoders in parallel, split by an interleaver, and decode by passing soft messages. LDPC codes do the same on a sparse graph. Turbo and LDPC reach within about a decibel of capacity; BCH stays a few dB away. Wi-Fi, 4G/5G data links and flash controllers  */
/* book Figure 7.9.1: The turbo encoder of the worked example: the block goes out once as it is, once through encoder 1 and once, reordered by the interleaver π, through encoder 2. Three bits per input bit give R = 1/3; deleting half of each parity stream gives R = 1/2. */
