/* book exam traps: Thinking a strong code can beat capacity. Turbo and LDPC codes approach the Shannon limit from below; nothing works above it. | Confusing code rate with redundancy when puncturing is given. Recount the bits actually transmitted, not the mother code's bits. | Writing dmin = 2t + 1 as exact. The design guarantees dmin ≥ 2t + 1; the true minimum distance may be larger. | Using n = 2m − 1 with the wrong m. n = 15 needs m = 4, not m = 15. | Making the turbo rate 1/4. The systematic bit goes out once, so two rate-1/2 encoders make 1/3, not 1/4. */
